** Overview

This file has been created to keep my ORG configuratio in one place.
Finally I decided to start using ORG files for emacs config - as this allows clearly desribe configuration
and take adventege of ORG workflow (TODO, checklist, etc).

** Known issues

For not this is working well - however there are some issues which I don't know how to quickly fix.

Short list:

- Org and Lisp code - sometimes idents changes and this requires fix it - ansible shows huge difference in diff
- Working with BIG ORG / List is starting be not easy as I expected
- Working with org.j2 - and change to org-mode - not always allows work with headlines as expected
  Sometimes I am not able expand headline
- Testing something quickly - I am doing directly on =~/.emacs.d/= files - and sometimes have no time
  to sync changes back - when I am doing this - this is taking a lot of time.

** Sync changes in ansible and emacs.d

As describe above sync between =ansible code= (source) and =~/.emacs.d= code is not easy.
I know that =emacs= can compare two buffers - however for now I am using =pycharm= (Allows me quickly compare changes)

Following command should be run

#+begin_src bash
  # Navigate to ansible emacs project (tmux)
  pycharm diff ~/.emacs.d/init-config.org ./roles/emacs-config/templates/init-config.org.j2
#+end_src

