** Custom configuration file                                                      :static:

When some settings has been adjusted in emacs, it saves all those changes in =~/.emacs= file.
Following configuration allows adjust this settings and have them in custom file.

This allow to keep separate dynamic configuration manages by user and dynamic configuration managed
by emacs it self.

For testing - please run =M-x customize=

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
  ;; Specify the custom file location
  (setq custom-file (expand-file-name "~/.emacs.d/custom-custom.el"))

  ;; Load the custom file if it exists
  (when (file-exists-p custom-file)
    (load custom-file))
#+end_src

