** Align comments in lines to the right                                           :static:

When one wants to have some comments on right, this function will align comments with =#= char.

#+begin_src text
  # Comments are not aligned
  some text here     # Comment1
  some text here with longer string  # Comment2

  # After selection and running this function =C-c #= all comments are aligned
  some text here       # Comment1
  some text here with longer string # Comment2
#+end_src

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
;; Select lines with comments after lines and use =C-c #=
;; This will align comments:
;; some text here                    # Comment1
;; some text here with longer string # Comment2
(defun mposl/align-to-hash-comments ()
  "Align `#` comments in the selected region to the right of the longest line."
  (interactive)
  (align-regexp (region-beginning) (region-end) "\\(\\s-+\\)#" 1 1 t))
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c #") 'mposl/align-to-hash-comments)
#+end_src

